From c7d3abc4d2427b5d2cde05297b79f7f30f07c817 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: liyingli <liyingli@amd.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:16:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [TransferEngine][ROCm] Add HipGemAllocator so pinned KV
 caches are not charged twice by KFD

amdgpu-dkms 6.18.4 through at least 7.1.9, and kernels without
torvalds/linux 9131cc85d0de ("drm/amdkfd: correct vram_available
calculation", v7.4-rc1), subtract vram_pin_size from the KFD allocation
limit without crediting KFD's own pins back. A hipMalloc buffer that a NIC
pins is then counted twice: once in kfd.vram_used and once as pinned.
After a prefill or decode server registers a KV cache larger than the VRAM
left after allocating it, every later device allocation of the process
fails; the first new HIP stream typically segfaults in
c10::hip::HIPStream::stream(). This holds for dma-buf and peer-memory
registration alike, so the KFD pin anchor (MC_HIP_KFD_PIN_FIX) only fixes
what hipMemGetInfo reports there, not what allocations get.

Add hip_gem_allocator.so, a torch CUDAPluggableAllocator backend exposed as
mooncake.allocator.HipGemAllocator. Each buffer is an amdgpu GEM BO created
on the GPU's render node and imported with hipImportExternalMemory; a
dma-buf import is not reserved in kfd.vram_used, so the pinned BO is charged
once. A one-page dma-buf MR pins it at allocation, so hipMemGetInfo covers
it from the start and it cannot be evicted before registration.

HIP reports no address range for imported memory, ROCr cannot export it as
a dma-buf, and HIP has no IPC handle for it, so the transfer engine looks
the buffer up in the allocator (mc_hip_gem_lookup, found with dlsym) and:
- registers it through the BO's own dma-buf whatever
  MOONCAKE_DISABLE_HIP_DMABUF says, failing if the kernel cannot;
- never through ibv_reg_mr: the amdgpu peer-memory client's amd_get_pages
  dereferences bo->kfd_bo, which is NULL for a GEM BO. Registration
  refuses that path and the KFD pin anchor skips these buffers;
- leaves it out of the HIP transport, so same-host transfers to it are
  routed over RDMA.
TENT gets the same: RocmPlatform::exportDmabuf returns the BO's dma-buf, and
the ibv_reg_mr fallback and MR warm-up skip GEM buffers.

isKernelDmabufSupported() is split so the kernel probe can be asked without
MOONCAKE_DISABLE_HIP_DMABUF. Add hip_gem_allocator_test (needs an AMD GPU
and a NIC taking dma-buf MRs), and document the allocator, its
MC_HIP_GEM_PIN_NIC, and where the KFD pin anchor does not help.

Signed-off-by: liyingli <liyingli@amd.com>
